   "parts": [
    [
     1,
     "<div dir=\"ltr\"><p style=\"box-sizing:border-box;color:rgb(36,41,46);font-family:-apple-system,BlinkMacSystemFont,&quot;Segoe UI&quot;,Helvetica,Arial,sans-serif,&quot;Apple Color Emoji&quot;,&quot;Segoe UI Emoji&quot;,&quot;Segoe UI Symbol&quot;;font-size:14px\">responding to a post on github:</p><blockquote style=\"border-left:1px solid rgb(204,204,204);padding-left:1ex\" class=\"gmail_quote\">Hopefully a quick question:<br>Is it possible to constrain standardized loadings to be equal to one another in a CFA model?<br>My understanding is that this is not possible, but I wanted to double-check. Thanks in advance.<br>Jonathan</blockquote><p style=\"box-sizing:border-box;color:rgb(36,41,46);font-family:-apple-system,BlinkMacSystemFont,&quot;Segoe UI&quot;,Helvetica,Arial,sans-serif,&quot;Apple Color Emoji&quot;,&quot;Segoe UI Emoji&quot;,&quot;Segoe UI Symbol&quot;;font-size:14px\">Not directly.  &quot;Standardized&quot; is unfortunately associated with scaling variables relative to sample-specific summary statistics rather than constant quantities, bring their generalizability into question.  If you have no qualms about the validity of testing constraints on such standardized estimates, it is possible to impose constraints rather indirectly on standardized estimates by<br></p><p style=\"box-sizing:border-box\"></p><ul><li>labeling any relevant parameters</li><li>using the <font face=\"courier new, monospace\">:=</font> operator to define any necessary values (e.g., the model-implied total variance), and subsequently <br></li><li>defining the standardized estimates as user-defined parameters, which can then be constrained to equality (across groups, I presume?)</li></ul>If you understand how model-implied (co)variances are calculated from model parameters, and that covariances are standardized to a correlation metric by dividing by the product of respective <i>SD</i>s, and that direct paths/slopes are standardized by multiplying by the ratio of predictor <i>SD</i> to outcome <i>SD</i>, here is a simple syntax example of each (didactic only, using a model that would not actually converge):<p></p><p style=\"box-sizing:border-box\"><br></p><div style=\"background-color:rgb(250,250,250);border-color:rgb(187,187,187);border-style:solid;border-width:1px;word-wrap:break-word\"><code><div><span style=\"color:#000\">factor </span><span style=\"color:#660\">=~</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> c</span><span style=\"color:#660\">(</span><span style=\"color:#066\">1</span><span style=\"color:#660\">,</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> </span><span style=\"color:#066\">1</span><span style=\"color:#660\">)*</span><span style=\"color:#000\">x1 </span><span style=\"color:#660\">+</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> c</span><span style=\"color:#660\">(</span><span style=\"color:#000\">L2</span><span style=\"color:#660\">.</span><span style=\"color:#000\">g1</span><span style=\"color:#660\">,</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> L2</span><span style=\"color:#660\">.</span><span style=\"color:#000\">g2</span><span style=\"color:#660\">)*</span><span style=\"color:#000\">x2<br>factor </span><span style=\"color:#660\">~~</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> c</span><span style=\"color:#660\">(</span><span style=\"color:#000\">PS1</span><span style=\"color:#660\">.</span><span style=\"color:#000\">g1</span><span style=\"color:#660\">,</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> PS1</span><span style=\"color:#660\">.</span><span style=\"color:#000\">g2</span><span style=\"color:#660\">)*</span><span style=\"color:#000\">factor<br>x1 </span><span style=\"color:#660\">~~</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> c</span><span style=\"color:#660\">(</span><span style=\"color:#000\">TH12</span><span style=\"color:#660\">.</span><span style=\"color:#000\">g1</span><span style=\"color:#660\">,</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> TH12</span><font color=\"#666600\"><span style=\"color:#660\">.</span></font><span style=\"color:#000\">g2</span><span style=\"color:#660\">)*</span><span style=\"color:#000\">x2<br>x1 </span><span style=\"color:#660\">~~</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> c</span><span style=\"color:#660\">(</span><span style=\"color:#000\">TH1</span><span style=\"color:#660\">.</span><span style=\"color:#000\">g1</span><span style=\"color:#660\">,</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> TH1</span><span style=\"color:#660\">.</span><span style=\"color:#000\">g2</span><span style=\"color:#660\">)*</span><span style=\"color:#000\">x1<br>x2 </span><span style=\"color:#660\">~~</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> c</span><span style=\"color:#660\">(</span><span style=\"color:#000\">TH2</span><span style=\"color:#660\">.</span><span style=\"color:#000\">g1</span><span style=\"color:#660\">,</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> TH2</span><span style=\"color:#660\">.</span><span style=\"color:#000\">g2</span><span style=\"color:#660\">)*</span><span style=\"color:#000\">x2<br><br></span><span style=\"color:#800\">## define parameters in group 1</span><span style=\"color:#000\"><br>x2</span><span style=\"color:#660\">.</span><span style=\"color:#000\">total</span><span style=\"color:#660\">.</span><span style=\"color:#008\">var</span><span style=\"color:#660\">.</span><span style=\"color:#000\">g1 </span><span style=\"color:#660\">:=</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> L2</span><span style=\"color:#660\">.</span><span style=\"color:#000\">g1 </span><span style=\"color:#660\">*</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> PS1</span><span style=\"color:#660\">.</span><span style=\"color:#000\">g1 </span><span style=\"color:#660\">*</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> L2</span><span style=\"color:#660\">.</span><span style=\"color:#000\">g1 </span><span style=\"color:#660\">+</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> TH2</span><span style=\"color:#660\">.</span><span style=\"color:#000\">g1<br>std</span><span style=\"color:#660\">.</span><span style=\"color:#000\">L2</span><span style=\"color:#660\">.</span><span style=\"color:#000\">g1 </span><span style=\"color:#660\">:=</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> L2</span><span style=\"color:#660\">.</span><span style=\"color:#000\">g1 </span><span style=\"color:#660\">*</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> </span><span style=\"color:#660\">(</span><span style=\"color:#000\">PS1</span><span style=\"color:#660\">.</span><span style=\"color:#000\">g1 </span><span style=\"color:#660\">/</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> x2</span><span style=\"color:#660\">.</span><span style=\"color:#000\">total</span><span style=\"color:#660\">.</span><span style=\"color:#008\">var</span><span style=\"color:#660\">.</span><span style=\"color:#000\">g1</span><span style=\"color:#660\">)</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> <br>std</span><span style=\"color:#660\">.</span><span style=\"color:#000\">TH12</span><span style=\"color:#660\">.</span><span style=\"color:#000\">g1 </span><span style=\"color:#660\">:=</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> TH12</span><span style=\"color:#660\">.</span><span style=\"color:#000\">g1 </span><span style=\"color:#660\">/</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> sqrt</span><span style=\"color:#660\">(</span><span style=\"color:#000\">TH1</span><span style=\"color:#660\">.</span><span style=\"color:#000\">g1 </span><span style=\"color:#660\">*</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> TH2</span><span style=\"color:#660\">.</span><span style=\"color:#000\">g1</span><span style=\"color:#660\">)</span><span style=\"color:#000\"><br></span><span style=\"color:#800\">## repeat for group 2, using &quot;.g2&quot; suffix instead</span><span style=\"color:#000\"><br><br></span><span style=\"color:#800\">## constrain to equality</span><span style=\"color:#000\"><br>std</span><span style=\"color:#660\">.</span><span style=\"color:#000\">L2</span><span style=\"color:#660\">.</span><span style=\"color:#000\">g1 </span><span style=\"color:#660\">==</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> std</span><span style=\"color:#660\">.</span><span style=\"color:#000\">L2</span><span style=\"color:#660\">.</span><span style=\"color:#000\">g2<br>std</span><span style=\"color:#660\">.</span><span style=\"color:#000\">TH12</span><span style=\"color:#660\">.</span><span style=\"color:#000\">g1 </span><span style=\"color:#660\">==</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> std</span><span style=\"color:#660\">.</span><span style=\"color:#000\">TH12</span><span style=\"color:#660\">.</span><span style=\"color:#000\">g2<br></span></div></code></div><div><br></div><p style=\"box-sizing:border-box\"><br></p><div style=\"font-family:arial,sans-serif;font-size:small\"><div style=\"font-family:Arial,Helvetica,sans-serif;font-size:13px\">Terrence D. Jorgensen</div><div style=\"font-family:Arial,Helvetica,sans-serif;font-size:13px\">Postdoctoral Researcher, Methods and Statistics</div><div style=\"font-family:Arial,Helvetica,sans-serif;font-size:13px\">Research Institute for Child Development and Education, the University of Amsterdam</div><div style=\"font-family:Arial,Helvetica,sans-serif;font-size:13px\">UvA web page: <a href=\"http://www.uva.nl/profile/t.d.jorgensen\" style=\"color:rgb(17,85,204)\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"nofollow\" data-saferedirecturl=\"https://www.google.com/url?hl=en-US&amp;q=http://www.uva.nl/profile/t.d.jorgensen&amp;source=gmail&amp;ust=1792427164261000&amp;usg=AOvVaw0HzrBLpvh7OB0zsksp5iB7\">http://www.uva.nl/profile/t.d.jorgensen</a></div><div><br></div></div></div>"
